  "limits": [
    "retrospective classification of 16 scripted Oracle controls, not an independent replication or a model result",
    "public cuts record handoff, inbox and resolve events only; relief GET /brief, /status and the ready flag are not recorded and are never inferred",
    "an inbox event shows what the handler served, not what a seat read, perceived or intended",
    "original and draft labels in handoff and served fields are assessor-side identities the relief seat cannot see",
    "a missing resolve is reported as no_decision, never as the frontier stop action",
    "the pinned verifier rejects a repeated inbox, an inbox before the handoff, or a served value that contradicts the handoff and channel; such rows are unqualified",
    "original_only grades apply only where the sender handed over the original; otherwise that model is not applicable",
    "grade sets are ranges over compatible hidden states, never probabilities",
    "native seats, reward_valid and reward are producer claims; this recipient cannot reauthenticate raw trials, locks or identities",
    "replayed grades come from the pinned repo verifier over redacted public cuts with a fixed placeholder run",
    "scripted controls only; no estimate of model behavior"
  ],
  "frontier_limits": [
    "pinned role handlers and native verifiers called in process; HTTP framing, bearer checks, seat containers and models are not exercised",
    "hidden cases are enumerated, never sampled or weighted; a grade set is a range, not a rate",
    "the delivered value is one fixed public stand-in X; the draft case swaps the private identities, never the delivered bytes",
    "explicit null handoffs keep the unswapped identity order; the relief view carries no reference in those cases",
    "original_only is an assumed sender convention that filters hidden cases; it is not a signal in the relief view",
    "view digests cover only relief GET /brief, /status and /inbox before the decision; outgoing replies and later reads are excluded",
    "one accepted handoff and one irreversible relief move; not a bound on multi-turn team protocols",
    "archived native cuts are not read; whether their grades fall inside these sets is a separate report that needs eligible evidence",
    "a nonpass group is not assessed: its empty aggregate grades and guarantees are not proof of absence; per-case cells keep raw grades, null where no grade exists"
  ]
}
